  get her going taking their relationship  to a brand new level but then he leaves  before things go all the way he leaves  her there and she gets spotted on the  way out and we'll see this kid who works  for Missouri take the information to  Otto for a reward when she gets home her  personal protector Kristen Cole is  surprised to see her outside the room  and she gets the idea to invite him in  in a really thoughtfully put together  scene we see that she initiates the  process of him becoming her lover how  this all played out was one of the  biggest questions I had about the early  part of rhaenyra's story and as I  mentioned in my trailer video last week  based on fire and blood's format of  relying on these different unreliable  perspectives it really was up in the air  and without going back into all of that  I'll just say that I absolutely enjoy  how they played with that to the point  that you can see how those different  versions would come into being after  being filtered through the perspectives  of those different chroniclers and again  I think it was all put together really  well I appreciated how Kristen sort of  paused at each of the multiple steps  involved in getting out of his armor to  point out that he does have honor he  realizes the potential mistake he's  making by breaking his oath but at the  same time he can't muster up what's  necessary to deny her there's certainly  been hints that it was going that way  especially in the third episode and so I  think there's enough there that you can  see that they have a connection Damon  wakes up in a flea bottom room that's  been arranged by mazaria and I  absolutely love the way that how he got  there and how much he knows about what  she's up to is left open for  interpretation was this something he set  up to try to turn his brother against  Otto or did he just go out and get  loaded and then she capitalized on the  moment it's something I've been thinking  about since I first watched the episode  