e gates he's escorted  forcefully by the kingsguard and left on  the floor of the throne room viserys  wants answers but he never gives any and  lets every chance he's given to deny it  pass right by it's all a little  maddening to watch until he proposes a  plan that makes it all make sense he  tells his brother to give him rhaenyra  to marry as a way to solve his problem  he frames it in a way that it doesn't  matter what people think because he's  the dragon and it's not hard for viserys  to see that it's not about rhaenera at  all but about the power she represents  it's a nice little echo of what she was  saying to Allison earlier Damon presents  this as a way to return the house of the  Dragon to its proper Glory his still  solution totally fits with what we've  seen of the character who as I mentioned  at the very beginning does a lot of  things that are hard to parse while he's  doing them a little bit later when  talking to Allison viserys will ask what  does he gain by admitting to something  he didn't do here and while it's not  clear if Damon actually knows what he's  trying to do or if he's just rolling  with the punches that come up because of  the way his chaos kind of creates all  these situations he always lands on the  side of trying to improve his position  in the end the king sends him away again  and as mentioned Allison does go to bat  for rhaenyra viserys maintains that  she's not innocent in this situation and  that her and Damon have the blood of the  Dragon which makes them restless and  chaotic still Alison is convinced by her  friend she swore to her that she remains  a maiden and she believes her when he  finally talks to his daughter he shows  her aegon's dagger which we find out  here also belong to Anar Targaryen which  is interesting because his daughter  danis's dream is what got them to leave  valyria before the Doom that's why they  left and subsequently is the reason that  all targaryens need to pay attention to  their dreams and